      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "PSBT input/output `Merge()` methods always return `true` unconditionally and have no failure paths. As a result, the return value checks in `PartiallySignedTransaction::Merge()` can never fail and are dead code.\r\nThis makes the `bool` return type and `[[nodiscard]]` misleading.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes both methods to return `void` and remove the return value checks. If at some point in the future the failure logic is needed, it can be introduced again. For now using `void` makes the current behavior easier to understand.",
